, \"handles stress very well\", \"good at assessing weather conditions\", \"excellent computer skills\". Concerns: \"can be grumpy\", \"can be uncooperative\". For Candidate C: \"can make correct decisions quickly\", \"is regarded as 100% reliable\", \"creates a positive atmosphere with his crew\". Concerns: \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"egocentric\", \"not very willing to further his education\". For Candidate D: \"responds to unexpected events adequately\", \"can concentrate very well\", \"solves problems extremely well\", \"takes responsibility seriously\". Concerns: \"regarded as arrogant\", \"relatively weak leadership skills\". Also \"arrogant\" and \"weak leadership\" are concerns.\n\nAgent 2's message: they said D is best, concerns are hot temper/arrogance, weak leadership, but they think manageable. They also said B's nasty remarks, C's communication issues, A's show-off.\n\nNow as Agent 1, we can either support D or propose another. Let's evaluate: Candidate C has 100% reliability and creates positive atmosphere, which is strong for crew cooperation. Decision quality is good (quick correct decisions). Technical competence? Not explicitly given, but can make correct decisions quickly suggests competence. Concerns: communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education. But reliability and crew atmosphere are strong. Candidate B is very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well, good at weather, computer skills. Concerns: grumpy, uncooperative. That could affect crew cooperation. Candidate A has anticipation, complex connections, spatial vision, leadership, but concerns: not good at criticism, unorganized. That could affect reliability and adaptability.\n\nCandidate D has problem solving, concentration, responsibility, but concerns: arrogance, weak leadership. Also \"responds adequately to unexpected events\" (maybe not as strong as \"handles stress very well\").\n\nWhich candidate overall? I think Candidate C's reliability and